3129-LOGBOOK.md:960:- ANOMALY: negative fixtures mutate the algorithm's **version suffix** — `curator-build-source-v2` appears in `build-receipt-v1/invalid-build-source-algorithm.json` and `install-marker-v2/invalid-build-source-algorithm.json`. An exclusion written against the exact `-source-v1` string is not enough; the exclusion must cover the whole `-source` namespace. First wiring of the absence guard went red on exactly this.
3130-LOGBOOK.md:1068:- EVIDENCE: revert-to-prove on both fixes. Restoring the scratch roots fails the containment tests with `temporary roots during the dry run = [curator-dry-run-2191237997]`; removing the global gates yields `Status:ok` with `outcome=would-preflight-and-build`, a staged artifact, and `build-skill tag v1 ... installed` on a run whose MCP/registry callback returned an error.
3131-LOGBOOK.md:1099:- FINDING: a naive "mutate the snapshot during `Inspect`" test does **not** discriminate the bracket — the final all-source recheck catches it anyway and the run still fails clean. The bracket is only observable through *where* the failure lands: with it, planning stops at that command (one inspection, zero planned builds, zero builder calls, error names `build-skill.alpha`); without it, a second command is planned and its miss is compiled first. The test asserts the former.
3132-LOGBOOK.md:1100:- FINDING: trust must be finalized even when nothing is compiled. A plan of pure cache hits establishes a session, skips the builder entirely, and previously reached live mutation with no re-verification at all. `TestCacheHitOnlyPlanStillFinalizesToolchainTrust` pins it.
3133-LOGBOOK.md:1108:- FINDING: build-source tokens are validated before cache lookup, but cache inspection is not bracketed by `Token.Use`, and `BuildPlan.Close` closes tokens without a final `Recheck`. A cache hit can therefore be selected from one source identity and then proceed to staging handoff/live materialization after the snapshot changes; misses likewise lack one final all-source recheck immediately before handoff.
3134-LOGBOOK.md:1118:- FINDING: `BuildOutcome` is deliberately a mirror of `buildcache.Result.DryRunOutcome()` rather than an independent enum — a plan must not be able to invent an outcome the read-only cache inspection did not report. `corrupt` and `unsupported` fail closed during planning; `would-rebuild-untrusted-cache` never exposes a reusable artifact path.
3135:LOGBOOK.md:1143:- DECISION: worker tests drive a real subprocess. `TestMain` gives the test binary the same hidden mode the manager has, and `testdata/stubgo` is a real compiled launcher inside a fingerprintable fake `GOROOT`. Consequence: measured `internal/godriver` coverage reads 72.1 % because worker-side statements execute out of process and are not attributed to the parent profile.
3136-LOGBOOK.md:1171:- DECISION: rejected shipping hardened-Linux-only — it would withhold the entire compiled-skill feature from the two platforms this release targets in exchange for a guarantee no supported host currently offers. Recorded in `decisions/0006-portable-manager-worker-execution.md`.
