3330:notes:Implementation directive: start from the independently accepted TASK-260720-1ljev5 candidate at /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/curator/.temp/TASK-260720-1ljev5/worktree, preserve it read-only, and work in this task own isolated worktree. Implement the complete CLI/currentness/repair surface across install, upgrade, dry-run, status, status --json, status --check and gc using existing protocol and code patterns. Enumerate every stable currentness/repair code from the accepted implementation/spec and keep human and JSON semantics mechanically aligned; preserve legacy output/exit behavior where compiled builds are not involved. Install/upgrade may repair invalid compiled state only through the accepted staged, atomic and GC-safe lifecycle, with deterministic diagnostics and manager-owned guidance; no auto-install or package-controlled executable/env/trust selection. Add focused unit/integration/race tests, macOS-native validation, Windows cross-build plus task-owned native checks over SSH alias win where applicable, and Linux cross-build/vet without claiming later native Linux validation. Do not stage, commit, publish, or overwrite predecessor/user changes. Attach task-scoped implementation and gate evidence, then hand off to independent review.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-5b614c, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-5b614c)\nCompiled diagnostics and repair surface implemented on the accepted 1ljev5 tree in .temp/TASK-260720-1nlmvv/worktree (base origin/main 17804ce, nothing staged or committed).\n\nNew: cmd/curator/builds.go (stable currentness vocabulary, per-command classification, redaction-aware rendering, repair notices, toolchain guidance) and internal/install/diagnostics.go (RedactDiagnostic: one-line, non-printable-stripped, absolute-path-redacted, 240-rune-bounded rendering of untrusted detail, applied by both status and PlannedBuild.Describe).\n\nstatus now reports one diagnostic row per active build command with driver, build_root, source_dir, build-source identity, native target, logical key, artifact path and cache outcome; --json adds an optional builds array and leaves the historical document byte-identical when the closure has no build commands; --check fails closed for every non-current code on both the declared-skill map and the build rows. install/upgrade print whether untrusted state was rebuilt or the previous installation was preserved. Result.BuildDiagnostic carries the stable go-v1 boundary code so guidance names CURATOR_GO, GOROOT and the tested families without suggesting PATH or a download.\n\nFixed a legacy regression: schema-1 markers were reported unsupported-marker since marker v2 landed.\n\nGates (real exit codes, standalone): gofmt 0, go build 0, go vet 0, go test ./... 0 (40 packages), golangci-lint v2.4.0 0 issues, go test -race ./internal/install -timeout 40m 0, go test -race ./cmd/curator ./internal/godriver 0, GOOS=windows/linux build 0, GOOS=linux vet 0. Expected red: GOOS=windows go vet exits 1 on internal/runtimestore (pre-existing and sibling-owned; identical on the untouched base; 0 when that package is excluded).\n\nCarry-forward findings in the attached notes: compiled installs are not idempotent (stageNode passes no BuildCurrentness), global status is not build-aware, internal/install needs -timeout 40m under -race, and one non-reproducible registry snapshot-skew flake.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-5b614c, pid=53894, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the CLI diagnostics/currentness/repair implementation; do not edit artifacts. Verify every task AC against the accepted composed base and challenge semantic claims, not just tests. Require one closed stable-code vocabulary with exact human/JSON agreement; status --check must be zero only for exact current and fail closed for every unknown/invalid/unsupported/missing/corrupt/drifted/racy state. Audit classification ordering and prove a logical-key mismatch can truthfully distinguish source, target, toolchain, command/build-root/policy causes rather than mislabeling several inputs. Verify cache-hit evidence binds receipt/path/hash, marker before/after race detection covers every relevant scope, currentness cannot promote a stale skill, transitive compiled commands are represented, referenced entries remain GC-safe, and repair through install/upgrade is gated, atomic, rollback-preserving, and never claims mutation during dry-run or failure. Fuzz/adversarially inspect RedactDiagnostic for Unix/Windows/UNC paths, URI/embedded path forms, invalid UTF-8, controls/zero-width characters, multiline and 240-rune bounds at both status and install surfaces. Check legacy schema acceptance cannot admit forged build state or regress old output/exit behavior; inspect hidden TestMain worker dispatch for production-equivalent identity checks and no visible/bypass command. Re-run focused unit/integration/race tests without treating increased timeout as correctness; validate macOS evidence, native Windows cross-compiled scope and honest missing git/Go limitations, and Linux crossbuild only. Adjudicate the reported repeated-install non-idempotence and missing global build-aware status against this task scope; reject if an AC-required workflow remains uncovered, otherwise require tracked follow-up. Publish TASK-260720-1nlmvv_review-verdict-cycle-1.md with ACCEPTED or exact CHANGES REQUESTED and route accordingly.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-13915e, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260728-13915e)\nREVIEW CYCLE 1 VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED. Blocking evidence is attached as TASK-260720-1nlmvv_review-verdict-cycle-1.md. Real corrupt and unsupported outcomes short-circuit before stable human/JSON build rows; unknown marker schemas and non-go-v1 marker drivers are rejected before their documented codes can be emitted; corrupt cache state is refused rather than atomically repaired; opaque logical-key drift is over-labelled as target/toolchain; token-only redaction leaks embedded and URI absolute paths and raw blocking errors bypass it. Independent focused normal/race/vet/format/diff gates pass, so this is semantic rework rather than a mechanical test failure. Route to implementation rework.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260728-13915e, pid=24079, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE (review cycle 1): Fix the four semantic blockers in the preserved implementation worktree; keep the green mechanical work and do not substitute classifier-only tests for production reachability. (1) Add a read-only diagnostic planning path for status that never mutates and converts real corrupt/unsupported/cache/toolchain/marker failures into one build row per affected command for both human and JSON output; ordinary status may report them without aborting, while --check alone fails nonzero. Use a two-stage untrusted marker envelope/read path so unknown schema and unsupported driver are diagnosable without trusting or activating their payload, or remove any code that cannot be made real; every documented code needs an end-to-end persisted-state test through the actual CLI. Missing/malformed/incompatible Go must also produce the stable machine row plus bounded guidance, not stderr-only output. (2) Make corrupt receipt and artifact state repairable by install and upgrade only after all gates. Build a replacement privately, preserve the live install and referenced cache entry until atomic commit, quarantine/replace under the manager lock, and roll back both cache and install on every injected failure. Add real install+upgrade E2E for corrupt receipt/artifact success and failure, including concurrent GC/currentness. (3) Stop labeling every opaque key mismatch as target/toolchain. Compare only facets actually persisted and emit specific codes only with direct evidence; use a stable non-attributing build-input-drift code for unresolved differences, with adversarial cases for build root, command, source_dir, target, toolchain and policy. Do not change frozen wire schemas silently. (4) Replace whitespace-token redaction with bounded scanning that catches embedded key=value, file:// and other URI forms, Unix, Windows drive and UNC paths, quotes/punctuation, invalid UTF-8, controls/format runes and multiline data. Apply the same function before every status, plan, Result.Errors, repair notice and toolchain detail surface; add leak canaries asserting no raw absolute path survives. Add real transitive compiled-status coverage. Explicitly document global-status and repeated-install boundaries; if existing task AC can support global build currentness without inventing a new CLI contract, include it, otherwise leave no false claim and use the orchestrator-owned follow-up. Re-run focused normal/race/lint/build/macOS and scoped native Windows tests plus Windows/Linux cross gates; do not repeat full 12-minute race suites when targeted coverage suffices. Hand off revised evidence only after production-path tests prove each stable state, atomic repair and redaction. No commit/stage/publish.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-5fd800, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260728-5fd800)\nCycle 2 rework landed against the CHANGES REQUESTED verdict. (1) Reachability: cmdStatus no longer discards compiled diagnostics when the read-only plan fails but still derived commands (legacy path unchanged when it did not); planBuilds records a toolchain-unavailable inventory row per active command with the stable go-v1 boundary code; markerRefusal separates unsupported-marker and unsupported-build-driver from invalid-marker without weakening marker.Read. (2) Corrupt cache is now a buildable miss, so install and upgrade repair it through quarantine-and-replace; blocking is now only unsupported and toolchain-unavailable. (3) build-target-mismatch became build-input-drift plus stable cause subcodes (build-root, target, unattributed) with an adversarial pass over every logical input component. (4) RedactDiagnostic rewritten as a bounded embedded/URI/Windows/UNC scanner and Result.failBuild routes every build-phase failure through it. Follow-ups filed: TASK-260729-2kaopg (global status build awareness, explicit exclusion documented in README) and TASK-260729-3jku56 (compiled install idempotence).\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260728-5fd800, pid=55213, exit=0)\nCONTINUATION DIRECTIVE after RUN-260728-5fd800 incomplete handoff: preserve .temp/TASK-260720-1nlmvv/worktree and all cycle-2 code/evidence. The implementation claims all four review blockers closed and non-race focused/build/vet/lint/full-test gates green. The first race sweep failed three internal/install tests with ENOSPC; the run then removed the shared Go build cache while concurrent reviewers were active, restarted internal/install race, and ended before that foreground result existed. The runtime killed the in-flight process; race.log contains only its header and no exit code. Do not clear or mutate shared caches again. Resume only after this Opus slot cooldown expires at 05:23:58 Asia/Tbilisi. Confirm no stale test remains, then run the required focused race gates as foreground standalone commands with real exit codes and adequate timeout, waiting to completion. Re-run only any gate invalidated by cache removal, attach cycle-2 continuation evidence, complete checklist truthfully and invoke developer handoff as the final board command. No new feature scope, stage, commit, publish, pin or host install.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260729-39026a, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260729-39026a)\nCYCLE-2 CONTINUATION COMPLETE (RUN after RUN-260729-39026a was killed mid-gate). No product code changed in this continuation; the tree in .temp/TASK-260720-1nlmvv/worktree is byte-identical to the cycle-2 handoff (no .go file is newer than the cycle-2 go test ./... log). No shared cache was cleared and no stale test of this task was running; the concurrent go test on this host belongs to TASK-260729-2kaopg worktree.\n\nThe three race gates that never produced a result are now complete, run sequentially as standalone processes with real exit codes: go test -race -timeout 30m ./internal/godriver = 0 (46.5s); go test -race -timeout 60m ./internal/install = 0 (764.3s); go test -race -timeout 60m ./cmd/curator = 0 (651.9s). Disk headroom 15Gi -> 14Gi, no ENOSPC.\n\nGates carried forward on the unchanged tree: gofmt 0, go build 0, go vet 0, golangci-lint v2.4.0 0 issues, go test ./... 0 (40 packages), GOOS=windows/linux build 0, GOOS=linux vet 0, native Windows install.test.exe redaction suite 0 and curator.test.exe classification suite 0. Expected red, reported as failing: GOOS=windows go vet exits 1 on internal/runtimestore (undefined: decodeHelperOutput) - pre-existing and sibling-owned, identical exit and message on the untouched accepted base. Not run: native Linux execution (no reachable Linux host with an approved Go toolchain).\n\nNew artifacts: TASK-260720-1nlmvv_implementation-notes-cycle-2.md (how each of the four blocking findings was closed), TASK-260720-1nlmvv_gate-evidence-cycle-2-continuation.md, TASK-260720-1nlmvv_gate-evidence-cycle-2.tar.gz (raw logs + runner). Logbook entry 2026-07-29 0554 records the corrupt-cache unrecoverability root cause, the unattributable cache key, the marker-refusal diagnostic split, the report-vs-verdict decision, the redaction rewrite, and the ENOSPC/PowerShell/timeout traps. Ready for review.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260729-39026a, pid=99020, exit=0)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 DIRECTIVE: Independently review the cycle-2 implementation and continuation evidence without editing producer artifacts. Recheck all four prior blockers against production-reachable CLI paths: complete and incomplete status plans must preserve legacy exit behavior while --check alone fails complete non-current reports; corrupt/unsupported/unusable-toolchain/unsupported-marker/unsupported-driver codes must be truthfully reachable or explicitly justified version/platform guards. Verify install and upgrade repair corrupt protected cache state only after every preflight gate, stage privately, preserve the old install on refusal, publish through the existing lock/quarantine path, and never adopt corrupt bytes. Challenge build-input drift attribution so it never claims evidence absent from the marker. Exercise redaction over embedded, URI, Unix, Windows-drive, UNC, multi-location, invalid-byte, bounded-error, and result-failure paths. Verify transitive compiled status, local/external compatibility, and no regression from the separately owned global-status task. Audit the attached real exit codes, no-post-gate source drift, race runs, native Windows evidence, expected-red Windows vet attribution, and disk/cache incident recovery. Run focused tests and the highest-value applicable gates without clearing shared caches; publish an exact task-scoped ACCEPTED or CHANGES REQUESTED verdict and route accordingly. No product edits, staging, commit, publication, pin, host install, or release mutation.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-6be57f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (run=RUN-260729-6be57f)\nREVIEW CYCLE 2 VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED. Exact evidence is attached as TASK-260720-1nlmvv_review-verdict-cycle-2.md. Corrupt/untrusted cache replacement occurs before transaction journaling and is not rolled back after later faults; build-related commit errors bypass bounded path redaction; toolchain-refusal rows omit the known go-v1 driver and validated build-source digest; and cache evidence is not revalidated across the final status verdict. Focused CLI/install tests, vet, formatting, and diff checks pass, so route to implementation rework.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (codex) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: codex (run=RUN-260729-6be57f, pid=44490, exit=0)\nREWORK CYCLE 3 DIRECTIVE (review cycle 2, queued behind exact Opus cooldown until 2026-07-29 06:25:25 +04): preserve all mechanically green cycle-2 code/evidence and close exactly four blockers from TASK-260720-1nlmvv_review-verdict-cycle-2.md. (1) Make corrupt/untrusted cache replacement transaction-owned or reversibly staged through every later target-stage, journal-prepare, and target-commit failure. The old referenced cache entry and installed scope must remain live until atomic commit; injected post-publication faults for both install and upgrade must restore exact cache and install bytes, with no winner/quarantine drift. (2) Route every build planning, staging, publication, Project, Global, and commit Result.Errors path through the one bounded RedactDiagnostic/failBuild surface; add absolute operation-private artifact/cache leak canaries and length/control bounds. (3) Populate missing/malformed/incompatible toolchain inventory rows with all identities already validated before the probe, especially driver=go-v1 and the exact build-source digest/object; assert human/JSON agreement end to end. (4) Bracket or revalidate cache receipt/artifact identity through the final status verdict, not only install-marker fingerprints; a same-marker concurrent cache removal, corruption, replacement, or GC race must produce build-state-changed and make --check fail, never publish a stale current/drift verdict. Add real concurrent cache/currentness regressions. Re-run focused normal/race gates and the smallest sufficient full checks without clearing shared caches; attach cycle-3 implementation and gate evidence and hand off for fresh independent review. No stage, commit, publish, pin, host install, release mutation, global-status edits, or unrelated refactor. Do not spawn this Opus before its exact eligible time.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: claude via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=claude; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260729-0e838f, max_parallel=20)\nspawn run started: [implementer] developer (claude) (run=RUN-260729-0e838f)\nCycle 3: all four cycle-2 blocking findings addressed. 1) Cache publication is reversible - buildcache.Revert plus PublicationResult.Quarantined, and runCommit puts the shared cache back on every post-publication failure whose journaled targets are all at their recorded preimage and whose keys no journal still references. E2E fault at the target-commit boundary proven for install and upgrade. 2) Build-cache commit failures carry a build-phase marker and go through the bounded redactor. 3) toolchain-unavailable rows carry driver plus validated build-source identity. 4) status re-takes the exact protected-cache lookup after classification and reports build-state-changed. Gates running.\nORCHESTRATOR GATE-ATTRIBUTION RECORD 2026-07-29 cycle 3: three overlapping full-suite attempts launched around 06:53-06:57 left orphaned package-test binaries after their wrappers exited; orchestrator terminated only those exact orphaned processes and excludes all three from evidence. The later single foreground go test ./... -count=1 -timeout 90m at 07:02 is authoritative: EXIT=0, cmd/curator 598.040s, install 291.061s, atomicity 420.504s, all packages pass. go test -race ./internal/install -count=1 is authoritative: EXIT=0, 680.563s. race-cmd-curator attempts 01 and 02 were operator-terminated immediately after violating the host-release barrier and are non-evidence; attempt 03 (go-build2623929337) was allowed to continue to avoid a retry loop and only its eventual real result may be cited. Do not represent any cancelled/orphaned run as a failure or pass. Any further race CLI/atomicity gate belongs on the optimized integrated candidate.\nagent completed: [implementer] developer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260729-0e838f, pid=67074, exit=0)\nGATE ATTRIBUTION FINALIZATION: race-cmd-curator attempt 03 left /tmp/race-cmd-03.log at zero bytes and no EXIT marker when RUN-260729-0e838f reached terminal; no matching Go/test process remains. It is therefore incomplete/non-evidence, not a pass or failure. Do not rerun it on the unoptimized tree. The next authoritative race-cmd gate is required on the fingerprint-optimized integrated candidate.\nFOCUSED TEST COMPLETION DIRECTIVE (cycle 3): Inspect the cycle-3 delta and TASK-260720-1nlmvv_implementation-notes-cycle-3.md; do not edit product code. Verify the sole unchecked criterion: cache publication is reversible on every post-publication failure, with install and upgrade end-to-end coverage. Run the exact focused tests named by the producer: TestRevertRestoresExactlyWhatAPublicationDisplaced, TestRevertFailsClosed, TestAFailedCommitRestoresTheBuildCacheItReplaced, TestARolledBackTargetCommitRestoresTheBuildCacheItReplaced, TestAnInFlightTransactionKeepsThePublishedCacheEntry, and TestInstallAndUpgradeRestoreTheCacheWhenTheCommitFails. Inspect production paths and fault injection for prepare, journal, and commit failures; also verify the four cycle-2 blockers are closed: reversible cache publication, bounded/redacted build-boundary commit errors, driver plus validated source digest in toolchain-refusal rows for human and JSON output, and fail-closed build-state-changed reporting under concurrent removal/corruption/replacement/protection loss. Do not rerun repository-wide or cmd race gates; authoritative cycle-3 gate attribution is already recorded and the cmd race gate is intentionally deferred to the integrated fingerprint candidate. If evidence proves the unchecked criterion, mark only that checklist item, attach a task-scoped tester outcome, and hand off to review. Otherwise attach exact failure evidence and route to development.\nspawn agent resolution: Agent selection: codex via explicit_override\nspawn launch composition: degraded_contract_unavailable; contract=agents-infra.child-launch-composition; provider=codex; schema=1; diagnostic=composition_contract_unavailable; bare child launch retained\nspawn queued: [tester] tester (codex) (run=RUN-260729-6